{"lines":[{"y":0.11173424036165835,"w":0.074231897989908813,"c":1,"h":0.016357100613687225,"t":"Reading","x":0.83531203441950197},{"c":1,"x":0.17695473366407857,"h":0.014723203769140158,"t":"READING PASSAGE 2","w":0.26954732259114589,"y":0.15547703167888871},{"t":"You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 14-26, which are based on Reading","w":0.72222223917643225,"x":0.17901233724589247,"h":0.017441860778592999,"y":0.18604651146484907,"c":1},{"x":0.17695473521182345,"h":0.014548579711374909,"t":"Passage 2 below.","y":0.20347467622066384,"w":0.14814814249674482,"c":1},{"c":1,"t":"Saving bugs to find new drugs","x":0.35583959708032237,"y":0.23451096394209059,"h":0.021714746320205425,"w":0.37269261678059901},{"h":0.01751034054795475,"c":1,"x":0.27572017610100508,"t":"Zoologist Ross Piper looks at the potential of insects in","w":0.53497940063476557,"y":0.26737338053488302},{"x":0.41126746141752996,"y":0.28177055358820513,"w":0.25363479614257817,"h":0.019359159525769054,"c":1,"t":"pharmaceutical research"},{"t":"A More drugs than you might think are derived from, or inspired by, compounds found","x":0.17690139224131249,"w":0.72851236979166678,"y":0.31392836846124506,"h":0.018639790295712166,"c":1},{"y":0.32973577010163257,"w":0.64826176961263016,"c":1,"t":"in living things. Looking to nature for the soothing and curing of our ailments is","h":0.018149961150296323,"x":0.21394690301776906},{"w":0.68125666300455734,"h":0.019163183385267124,"x":0.21800435255457312,"t":"nothing new - we have been doing it for tens of thousands of years. You only have","c":1,"y":0.34396651596806294},{"t":"to look at other primates - such as the capuchin monkeys who rub themselves with","h":0.014557139752750858,"x":0.21604938813170918,"y":0.36189634874395127,"w":0.68724278767903646,"c":1},{"c":1,"t":"toxin-oozing millipedes to deter mosquitoes, or the chimpanzees who use noxious","y":0.37634665406638512,"h":0.018499804048571988,"x":0.21598987556117302,"w":0.6770857238769532},{"h":0.013081395583944611,"y":0.393895348717618,"x":0.21604939171852797,"w":0.66255142211914064,"c":1,"t":"forest plants to rid themselves of intestinal parasites - to realise that our ancient"},{"h":0.013089955625320671,"t":"ancestors too probably had a basic grasp of medicine.","c":1,"x":0.22016460034119403,"y":0.40842167238898996,"w":0.44650207519531249},{"t":"C","w":0.018518517812093099,"h":0.014534883982160851,"x":0.17695473276062013,"y":0.57703488344496612,"c":1},{"w":0.6380396525065104,"c":1,"y":0.43710328546936583,"t":"Pharmaceutical science and chemistry built on these ancient foundations and","x":0.21804647587556589,"h":0.018025809940657167},{"c":1,"x":0.21800199077065885,"w":0.67923110961914057,"t":"perfected the extraction, characterisation, modification and testing of these natural","y":0.45230074985890178,"h":0.019443316510203923},{"t":"products. Then, for a while, modern pharmaceutical science moved its focus away","c":1,"w":0.67717193603515624,"x":0.21799549758080008,"h":0.019251748164775595,"y":0.46823742156029269},{"y":0.4821722716728114,"w":0.66893595377604176,"h":0.020724257254628675,"t":"from nature and into the laboratory, designing chemical compounds from scratch.","x":0.21799200790743603,"c":1},{"w":0.68119867960611979,"y":0.49949578490655444,"h":0.017495108156237893,"t":"The main cause of this shift is that although there are plenty of promising chemical","x":0.21804826314476525,"c":1},{"x":0.21797329263369022,"w":0.68139770507812492,"t":"compounds in nature, finding them is far from easy. Securing sufficient numbers of","h":0.021416642781000417,"y":0.51326690326373348,"c":1},{"h":0.018336592630446957,"c":1,"y":0.53027583387670596,"x":0.21803728159208541,"t":"the organism in question, isolating and characterising the compounds of interest,","w":0.66474197387695311},{"y":0.54596428185794599,"t":"and producing large quantities of these compounds are all significant hurdles.","w":0.6420950317382812,"x":0.21803336569385712,"h":0.017109222771562571,"c":1},{"t":"Laboratory-based drug discovery has achieved varying levels of success,","c":1,"w":0.60493825276692703,"h":0.014543444023536689,"y":0.57703488356955079,"x":0.2181070057446963},{"x":0.21804657151105838,"h":0.017041706224493192,"t":"something which has now prompted the development of new approaches focusing","y":0.59218258971447624,"w":0.6770796712239584,"c":1},{"x":0.2180428667989969,"h":0.017372533485942809,"c":1,"t":"once again on natural products. With the ability to mine genomes for useful","y":0.60748897247073275,"w":0.61947682698567708},{"y":0.62199664420299927,"w":0.68334955851236989,"c":1,"h":0.018197667893588343,"x":0.21800652689434191,"t":"compounds, it is now evident that we have barely scratched the surface of nature's"},{"c":1,"y":0.63779085016097092,"t":"molecular diversity. This realisation, together with several looming health crises,","x":0.22007609884742285,"h":0.01877155124228469,"w":0.65654032389322903},{"t":"such as antibiotic resistance, has put bioprospecting - the search for useful","h":0.018477078180571538,"w":0.62156784057617187,"c":1,"y":0.65381096274685346,"x":0.21803373357730474},{"y":0.67005813939273284,"w":0.39094650268554687,"x":0.22016460873953111,"c":1,"t":"compounds in nature - firmly back on the map.","h":0.014570836043610647},{"w":0.66049382527669254,"x":0.21399176983764817,"h":0.013250883392226132,"t":"Insects are the undisputed masters of the terrestrial domain, where they occupy","y":0.70053003532665037,"c":1},{"h":0.018511717114487847,"c":1,"x":0.21803344734098726,"t":"every possible niche. Consequently, they have a bewildering array of interactions","y":0.71470109605905763,"w":0.66683822631835932},{"w":0.65649363199869792,"y":0.73060977653813663,"h":0.015580990570032371,"c":1,"x":0.22011170196588181,"t":"with other organisms, something which has driven the evolution of an enormous"},{"y":0.74705535917857746,"t":"range of very interesting compounds for defensive and offensive purposes. Their","w":0.66460906982421875,"x":0.22016460079719158,"c":1,"h":0.013250883392226132},{"x":0.21802121410459335,"w":0.65656372070312496,"h":0.017720471843813868,"y":0.76158575375728499,"t":"remarkable diversity exceeds that of every other group of animals on the planet","c":1},{"c":1,"w":0.65853764851888019,"x":0.22217382607825376,"y":0.77757687931010211,"h":0.014145598394710635,"t":"combined. Yet even though insects are far and away the most diverse animals in"},{"w":0.68529642740885421,"t":"existence, their potential as sources of therapeutic compounds is yet to be realised.","h":0.016001258778207017,"y":0.79241319572705815,"c":1,"x":0.22215443354886588},{"y":0.86918604633461338,"h":0.013081395583944722,"c":1,"x":0.88271604949522875,"t":"63","w":0.024691357612609877}],"h":3395,"w":2400}